From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Set WPA authentication algorithm before RSN validation

RSN and PMKID validation uses the WPA state machine's authentication
algorithm. Copying sta->auth_alg before validation makes that value
available to the checks instead of assigning it afterwards.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
+++ b/src/ap/drv_callbacks.c
@@ -634,6 +634,7 @@ int hostapd_notif_assoc(struct hostapd_d
 					     &sta->mld_info);
 		}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+		wpa_auth_set_auth_alg(sta->wpa_sm, sta->auth_alg);
 		res = wpa_validate_wpa_ie(hapd->wpa_auth, sta->wpa_sm,
 					  hapd->iface->freq,
 					  ie, ielen,
